1
00:00:07,400 --> 00:00:09,539
One night, long after
Trurl had gone to bed,

2
00:00:09,579 --> 00:00:12,551
somebody hammered on his door
hard enough to shake it loose.

3
00:00:13,051 --> 00:00:14,741
He drew the bolts, half asleep.

4
00:00:14,781 --> 00:00:18,575
A ship shaped like an enormous
pyramid had landed on his front lawn.

5
00:00:18,975 --> 00:00:21,532
Porters hurried down its
ramp with sacks of gifts,

6
00:00:21,572 --> 00:00:25,311
and stacked them so fast that the
sacks were soon taller than the house.

7
00:00:25,711 --> 00:00:28,683
Through a gap in the sacks came
a knight of polished armor,

8
00:00:28,723 --> 00:00:31,991
with jeweled eyes, swept-back
antennas, and a stole of diamonds.

9
00:00:32,391 --> 00:00:34,712
THE GRAND SENESCHAL: Do
I have the pleasure of

10
00:00:34,752 --> 00:00:37,062
addressing Trurl, the
celebrated constructor?

11
00:00:37,362 --> 00:00:40,042
TRURL: Yes. Sorry. I was
asleep. Come in, come in.

12
00:00:40,742 --> 00:00:43,207
THE GRAND SENESCHAL:
My king sends for you.

13
00:00:43,247 --> 00:00:46,392
His son is sick with love,
and you alone can cure him.

14
00:00:48,492 --> 00:00:49,735
Trurl put on a bathrobe.

15
00:00:49,775 --> 00:00:53,517
The knight sat down across from him,
and his helmet purred like a cat.

16
00:00:53,917 --> 00:00:57,139
THE GRAND SENESCHAL: First, a
small advance on your reward.

17
00:00:57,439 --> 00:01:01,241
He drew his sword, and tapped Trurl
on the shoulder once for every title.

18
00:01:01,541 --> 00:01:05,728
THE GRAND SENESCHAL: Duke of the Lesser
Drizzle. Warden of the Eleven Spoons.

19
00:01:05,768 --> 00:01:09,117
Baron Upside, and Baron Downside.
Keeper of the Royal Hiccup.

20
00:01:09,517 --> 00:01:13,185
Outside, the sacks had climbed past
the window, and the room went dim.

21
00:01:13,985 --> 00:01:16,588
TRURL: Matters of the
heart are not my field.

22
00:01:17,388 --> 00:01:19,836
THE GRAND SENESCHAL: The
prince loves Amarandina,

23
00:01:19,876 --> 00:01:22,020
the only daughter of
the Emperor next door.

24
00:01:22,060 --> 00:01:26,082
Our two kingdoms have hated each other
for centuries, so her father will refuse.

25
00:01:26,122 --> 00:01:28,712
A year has gone by, and
the prince is wasting away.

26
00:01:29,112 --> 00:01:31,615
Trurl looked out through
the gap in the sacks.

27
00:01:31,655 --> 00:01:34,530
Rows of soldiers stood on
his lawn, perfectly still.

28
00:01:34,930 --> 00:01:37,479
TRURL: Well. If the king
wishes it, then naturally.

29
00:01:37,879 --> 00:01:40,042
The knight clapped his hands with a clang.

30
00:01:40,082 --> 00:01:43,805
Armored retainers carried Trurl
aboard, and the ship rose into the sky.

31
00:01:46,205 --> 00:01:49,369
In the royal gardens stood
the Temple of Contemplation.

32
00:01:49,409 --> 00:01:52,865
In three weeks Trurl filled it
with cables, glowing screens,

33
00:01:52,905 --> 00:01:56,168
rose petals and perfume, and
named it the femfatalatron.

34
00:01:56,568 --> 00:02:00,366
Whoever stepped inside would feel
every charm in the universe at once.

35
00:02:00,406 --> 00:02:02,764
On the front, behind
glass, were the dials.

36
00:02:03,164 --> 00:02:07,079
TRURL: Power, forty megamors.
Efficiency, ninety-six percent.

37
00:02:07,119 --> 00:02:08,999
And this is the rapturometer.

38
00:02:09,399 --> 00:02:12,146
There was also an ardor
damper, a sigh condenser,

39
00:02:12,186 --> 00:02:14,802
and a swoon regulator,
each with its own knob.

40
00:02:15,302 --> 00:02:19,293
Forty elderly peers took four hours to
push the prince along the garden path.

41
00:02:19,333 --> 00:02:23,259
He kicked and butted them all the way,
so they pushed with feather pillows.

42
00:02:24,059 --> 00:02:26,065
TRURL: Every dial, all the way up.

43
00:02:28,165 --> 00:02:30,375
THE MACHINE: Five. Four.
Three. Two. One. Begin.

44
00:02:31,175 --> 00:02:31,814
The hum rose.

45
00:02:31,854 --> 00:02:34,689
Every needle climbed until
it pressed against its stop,

46
00:02:34,729 --> 00:02:36,244
and stayed there for an hour.

47
00:02:36,744 --> 00:02:38,064
Trurl watched and waited.

48
00:02:38,104 --> 00:02:40,187
He only made sure nothing went too far,

49
00:02:40,227 --> 00:02:43,111
so the prince would not fall
for the machine instead.

50
00:02:43,711 --> 00:02:45,258
At last the trapdoor opened.

51
00:02:45,298 --> 00:02:48,319
Out of a cloud of perfume,
across crushed rose petals,

52
00:02:48,359 --> 00:02:50,230
the prince stumbled, and fainted.

53
00:02:51,330 --> 00:02:53,041
PRINCE PANTAGOON: Amarandina.

54
00:02:54,241 --> 00:02:56,689
Trurl pressed the
rapturometer to his forehead.

55
00:02:56,729 --> 00:02:59,654
It read one hundred and seven,
and then the glass burst,

56
00:02:59,694 --> 00:03:01,865
and the mercury ran out, still trembling.

57
00:03:04,565 --> 00:03:07,222
That night some stonemasons
crept inside to see

58
00:03:07,262 --> 00:03:09,861
how it worked, and
switched it on by accident.

59
00:03:09,901 --> 00:03:13,459
They came out smoking, and
somebody sent for the fire brigade.

60
00:03:14,059 --> 00:03:18,389
Next Trurl built a heavier machine, all
iron, with bigger parts and bigger dials.

61
00:03:18,989 --> 00:03:21,200
THE MACHINE: Five. Four.
Three. Two. One. Begin.

62
00:03:21,700 --> 00:03:25,067
The needles climbed faster this
time, and hit their stops harder.

63
00:03:25,767 --> 00:03:27,310
PRINCE PANTAGOON: Amarandina!

64
00:03:27,810 --> 00:03:30,973
Trurl paced his room for miles,
read every manual he owned,

65
00:03:31,013 --> 00:03:32,696
and threw each one at the wall.

66
00:03:33,596 --> 00:03:38,243
TRURL: Every dial measured the prince.
The trouble was never inside the prince.

67
00:03:40,743 --> 00:03:42,642
In the morning he asked to see the king.

68
00:03:43,042 --> 00:03:46,620
TRURL: Your Majesty, I used the
strongest methods there are.

69
00:03:46,660 --> 00:03:49,152
I could build him an imitation Amarandina,

70
00:03:49,192 --> 00:03:52,388
but sooner or later he would
hear about the real one.

71
00:03:53,188 --> 00:03:57,633
He will not stop loving her as long
as he lives. So he has to marry her.

72
00:03:58,433 --> 00:04:01,072
KING PROTUBERON: Impossible.
The Emperor will never agree.

73
00:04:01,372 --> 00:04:05,041
TRURL: Not even if he had to? If he
were beaten, and begged for peace?

74
00:04:05,341 --> 00:04:08,755
KING PROTUBERON: A war, for my son’s
wedding? Two great kingdoms in blood?

75
00:04:08,795 --> 00:04:09,729
Out of the question.

76
00:04:10,129 --> 00:04:13,934
TRURL: That is the answer I hoped
for. But not every war is the same.

77
00:04:14,334 --> 00:04:18,451
Trurl leaned in and whispered his plan,
and slowly the king’s face brightened.

78
00:04:18,851 --> 00:04:21,456
KING PROTUBERON: Go and do it,
stranger. And good luck to you.

79
00:04:23,856 --> 00:04:27,270
TRURL: Not one of their people
will be killed. Quite the reverse.

80
00:04:28,070 --> 00:04:32,318
The royal foundries began casting huge
cannons, and nobody knew what for.

81
00:04:32,358 --> 00:04:35,824
They were set all around the
planet, disguised as defenses.

82
00:04:36,324 --> 00:04:39,094
Trurl lived in the royal
laboratory, day and night,

83
00:04:39,134 --> 00:04:41,338
over cauldrons that bubbled and gurgled.

84
00:04:41,838 --> 00:04:44,992
A spy at the door would have
heard only small cooing sounds,

85
00:04:45,032 --> 00:04:48,067
and seen assistants running
past with armfuls of diapers.

86
00:04:50,667 --> 00:04:54,084
Seven days later, at midnight,
the cannons lifted their muzzles

87
00:04:54,124 --> 00:04:57,526
toward the pale white star where
the Emperor ruled, and fired.

88
00:04:58,026 --> 00:04:59,219
They fired no shells.

89
00:04:59,259 --> 00:05:03,488
They fired babies, wrapped up soft,
each one on its own small parachute.

90
00:05:04,088 --> 00:05:07,316
The babies landed gently, by the
thousand, and crawled everywhere,

91
00:05:07,356 --> 00:05:09,584
and grew, and there were
always more of them.

92
00:05:10,084 --> 00:05:13,042
The nurseries filled, then the
streets, then the treasury.

93
00:05:13,082 --> 00:05:14,943
The Emperor’s economy began to sink.

94
00:05:15,443 --> 00:05:19,134
And still the bundles came down,
plump and cheerful, diapers flapping.

95
00:05:20,134 --> 00:05:23,018
THE EMPEROR: Enough. Tell him
the prince may marry my daughter.

96
00:05:25,818 --> 00:05:27,777
The cannons were plugged and stored.

97
00:05:27,817 --> 00:05:31,594
Just in case, Trurl took the
femfatalatron apart with his own hands.

98
00:05:32,494 --> 00:05:34,627
TRURL: Nobody turns this on again.

99
00:05:35,627 --> 00:05:38,967
At the wedding feast Trurl was
best man, dressed in emeralds

100
00:05:39,007 --> 00:05:42,613
from collar to cuff, and led the
toasts with a ceremonial baton.

101
00:05:43,013 --> 00:05:45,324
THE GUESTS: To the prince and Amarandina!

102
00:05:45,924 --> 00:05:47,454
PRINCE PANTAGOON: Amarandina.

103
00:05:48,354 --> 00:05:50,894
Then Trurl loaded his
rocket with all the titles

104
00:05:50,934 --> 00:05:53,245
both monarchs had given
him, and flew home.

